* sg13g2-bandgap -- core-open-loop-bias-pex bench body for the `klt sim`
* harness (issue #278, the remaining half of #275). Instantiated by
* sim/core-open-loop-bias-pex/run_klt_sim.sh, which substitutes @@OSDI_DIR@@
* and @@PEX_BODY@@. The DUT half -- every device and every wire parasitic --
* is GENERATED by sim/tools/gen_pex_netlist_body.py (with this bench's
* per-leg ammeters cut in via --ammeter) and rides in through the include;
* nothing in this file transcribes an extraction card. Edit the fixture
* here, the DUT in the generator's two committed inputs.
*
* `klt sim` netlist-body convention (klt sim --help, "Netlist convention"):
* this file is a circuit BODY. It carries no `.lib`, no `.temp`, no
* `.options temp=`, no analysis card and no `.end` -- `klt sim` generates
* all of those around an `.include` of this file, per corner.
*
* ONE DELIBERATE DEVIATION, same as every `klt sim` body in this repo: the
* `.control` block below. SG13G2's MOS and resistor compact models are OSDI
* (Verilog-A compiled by sim/tools/build-osdi.sh) and must be loaded by
* `pre_osdi` BEFORE the netlist is parsed; `klt sim`'s generated `.control`
* block has no extension point for an engine preload command (filed
* upstream, klayout-tools#2666 -- see sim/harness/README.md "Upstream
* friction"). Verified on ngspice 46 by sim/harness/probe/run_probe.sh.
.control
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/psp103_nqs.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/mosvar.osdi
pre_osdi @@OSDI_DIR@@/r3_cmc.osdi
.endc

* Solver options. The request `options` object is the runner's (timeout,
* artifacts, worker pool) and carries no engine-option passthrough, so a
* SPICE `.options` setting belongs in the body. `reltol=5e-3` is issue
* #264's setting for the trim-bearing DUT. `rshunt`/`gmin` are deliberately
* ABSENT -- the previous hand-transcribed template carried rshunt=1e9
* gmin=1e-9 as convergence aids, and issue #278 drops them: against the
* 255-unit ladder's interior nodes they leak ~0.55 uA out of the output
* branch, a ~37 mV settled-vref artifact at code 128 (see
* sim/closed-loop-vref-boxtc-trim/README.md "Solver options"). The 0->VDD
* history that replaced them is nothing: this is a cold DC bench whose
* claim is measured 40 ns into a 50 ns transient (the `.op`-substitute
* shape sim/harness/README.md documents). `temp`/`tnom` are NOT set here:
* `klt sim` emits the corner's own `.temp` card, and tnom defaults to 27.
.options reltol=5e-3

* Resident-vector save (issue #278 work item 3) -- deliberately ABSENT
* here. The card is required on the 3 ms transient benches, where the
* all-nodes x all-timesteps startup allocation is the hazard; this bench's
* window is 50 ns, so that hazard does not apply -- and a `.save` list
* disables `par('...')` inside `.meas ... find` (ngspice rewrites the
* expression to an internal `pa_<n>` parameter and then fails to find it
* as a vector; verified on ngspice 46). Five of this bench's columns are
* derived, so the derived-`.meas` form wins here.

* Supply/ground. `Vvdd`'s dc value is a placeholder: `klt sim` overrides it
* per corner with an `alter Vvdd=<v>` card generated from the request's
* `corners.supply_v` axis, which is why the rail source has to be a named,
* alterable element here.
Vvdd vdd 0 dc 3.30
Vvss vss 0 dc 0

* Ground reference for every net's own parasitic capacitance in the
* generated body (the extractor's far-plate convention). NOT the same net
* as vss: this is a DC bench, and the extraction itself already carries
* its own 1 TOhm DC-only tie (`Rvsubs_dctie vsubs 0 1e+12` rides in the
* generated wire-parasitic block), which guarantees zero DC effect while
* giving the far plate a DC path -- the same fixture the hand-transcribed
* template relied on, now part of the extraction. Nothing extra is needed
* here, and duplicating the device name would be a hard ngspice error.

* FIXTURE 1 -- open-loop mirror bias, same convention as
* sim/core-open-loop-bias (no error amplifier in this bench -- issue #9's
* scope cut): a diode-connected replica of the mirror device, carrying a
* 5 uA reference, sets the shared gate net. The refreshed extraction names
* that gate net `fb` itself (the pre-#272 extractions left it anonymous),
* so no rename fixture is needed any more.
XM0 fb fb vdd vdd sg13_hv_pmos w=10u l=1u ng=1 m=1
Ibias fb vss dc 5u

* DUT -- generated PEX body (devices + wire parasitics + this bench's
* per-leg ammeters, cut into the load-side terminal of each mirror leg by
* gen_pex_netlist_body.py --ammeter, the only place a terminal can be cut
* correctly).
.include @@PEX_BODY@@
